  "text": "@Injectable decorator in TypeScript is used to mark a class or a method as a service dependency. When used with a class, it tells the dependency injection (DI) system that the class itself needs to be resolved into an instance, typically through a factory or a provider that can instantiate the class.\n\nFor example, in the given code snippet:\n\n@Injectable\nclass Chart {\n  private context: CanvasRenderingContext2D;\n\n  constructor(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, private chartRef: ChartRef) {}\n\n  ngOnInit(): void {\n    this.chartRef.chartInstance = new Chart(context) as any;\n  }\n}\n\n@Injectable\nclass Chart {\n  private context: CanvasRenderingContext2D;\n\n  // This constructor is not using @Injectable decorator, so it's just another class constructor\n  constructor(private chartRef: ChartRef) {}\n\n  // Other methods and logic to create the chart instance\n  createChart(context: CanvasRenderingContext2D) {\n    this.context = context;\n    const chartInstance = new Chart(context) as any; // Careful: direct instantiation of the Chart class\n    // Return the chart instance somewhere\n  }\n}\n\nThe @Injectable decorator is used in the createChart method of the Chart class, which means the class/chartRef is marked as a dependency that needs to be provided and can be injected when needed. This approach is beneficial for isolating the class and managing its dependencies more cleanly, allowing for easier testing as you can control the instantiation and dependencies manually during testing cycles.\n\n@Injectable\nclass Chart {\n  private context: CanvasRenderingContext2D;\n\n  constructor(context: CanvasRenderingContext2D, private chartRef: ChartRef) {\n    this.context = context;\n  }\n\n  createChart(): any {\n    // If you need to create a chart in createChart, you can do it like this:\n    const chartInstance = new Chart(context) as any; // Direct instantiation of the Chart class to create the chart instance\n    // Now chartInstance should have the properties and methods of the Chart class.\n    // Return the chart instance somewhere\n    return chartInstance;\n  }\n}\n\n# How We Work\n\nSafety Associés provides end-to-end solutions from initial review through post-construction monitoring, designed to maximize protection for clients and their projects. The Safety Department Commentary Agreement breaks down Safety's Predictive Processes and Operations into 7 groups:\n\n安全 Associates provides end-to-end solutions from initial review through post-construction monitoring, designed to maximize protection for clients and their projects. The Safety Department Commentary Agreement breaks down Safety's Predictive Processes and Operations into 7 groups:\n\n建设工程安全隐患分析决策 4. 提供客户项目的安全分析、隐患决策及安全跟踪 5. 管理工程安全、为客户设计安全监控系统",
